{"title":"2021 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 19","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1_(Inverse_Trigonometric_Functions)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1 (Inverse Trigonometric Functions)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Equality_Conditions)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Equality Conditions)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Cofunction_Identity)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Cofunction Identity)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4_(Graphs_and_Analyses)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4 (Graphs and Analyses)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_5_(No_Graphing)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5 (No Graphing)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn_(Using_Triangle_Inequality_&amp;_Trigonometry)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn (Using Triangle Inequality &amp; Trigonometry)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_(Quick_and_Easy)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution (Quick and Easy)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>How many solutions does the equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/b/4fb433e234d30bde42f328004d6b7080465575ac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin \\left( \\frac{\\pi}2 \\cos x\\right)=\\cos \\left( \\frac{\\pi}2 \\sin x\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"226\" height=\"33\" /> have in the closed interval <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/e/ece27ba559bd93cdf2416aa0f88fc8d7d85e5791.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[0,\\pi]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"40\" height=\"20\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/5/045202f3d055baf59b5ca890c1b58c80483c3c69.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) }0 \\qquad \\textbf{(B) }1 \\qquad \\textbf{(C) }2 \\qquad \\textbf{(D) }3\\qquad \\textbf{(E) }4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"353\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_1_.28Inverse_Trigonometric_Functions.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1_(Inverse_Trigonometric_Functions)\">Solution 1 (Inverse Trigonometric Functions)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1 (Inverse Trigonometric Functions)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The ranges of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/c/fec8449ecbb9aea276fc7b322868ac9b194544fb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\pi}2 \\sin x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"56\" height=\"34\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/7/a777c0caa103f45612da7ceb63ca62d60cad670e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\pi}2 \\cos x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"58\" height=\"34\" /> are both <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/1/a9170cca00e4a24c4e6d2a174dc3152583601428.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left[-\\frac{\\pi}2, \\frac{\\pi}2 \\right],$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"79\" height=\"35\" /> which is included in the range of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/4/4f480e90caf523c49d4010a9990f966eac653424.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\arcsin,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"50\" height=\"15\" /> so we can use it with no issues.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/5/785c92ef7dd45bf84ae4bcfbd3ff8ce2fa1f6b84.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} \\frac{\\pi}2 \\cos x &amp;= \\arcsin \\left( \\cos \\left( \\frac{\\pi}2 \\sin x\\right)\\right) \\\\ \\frac{\\pi}2 \\cos x &amp;= \\arcsin \\left( \\sin \\left( \\frac{\\pi}2 - \\frac{\\pi}2 \\sin x\\right)\\right) \\\\ \\frac{\\pi}2 \\cos x &amp;= \\frac{\\pi}2 - \\frac{\\pi}2 \\sin x \\\\ \\cos x &amp;= 1 - \\sin x \\\\ \\cos x + \\sin x &amp;= 1. \\end{align*}\" width=\"325\" height=\"159\" />\nThis only happens at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/e/b9ee0ae966d8293f3a17707d5f7d841631f720b5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 0, \\frac{\\pi}2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"65\" height=\"33\" /> on the interval <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/1/8a18c184a0b45c0a3996945b662b19e0f50328ad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[0,\\pi],$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"42\" height=\"18\" /> because one of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/b/6fb300dacfcde1b57ad070409262b1743e0cd966.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"24\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/5/bb5e108fdc4bf4fb6151cb922992f23bc6c35985.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos$\" width=\"24\" height=\"8\" /> must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and the other <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/4/604c735470dd0152ca1cff75fe26eadf5cef7f49.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> Therefore, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/c/08c183761fd0ecf4de322d4dfd5af3320bce4bbe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(C) }2}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"59\" height=\"28\" />\n</p><p>~Tucker\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Equality_Conditions.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Equality_Conditions)\">Solution 2 (Equality Conditions)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Equality Conditions)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Hmmm, those values <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/9/08985694eb667e303b622c19e1c24457edf4ebca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\pi}{2} \\cos(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"69\" height=\"34\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/d/97df26d3f50f5fc3480d9f681a6bf0677b36ac1b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\pi}{2} \\sin(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"67\" height=\"34\" /> look scary. If only there were a way to simplify it...\n</p><p>Well, thanks to trigonometry, we can! Notice the equality condition <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/5/36514b0c858dd0131dc5365560672d7077e66a3a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\cos(x)\\right) = \\cos\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\sin(x)\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"253\" height=\"35\" />. Now, say <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/4/df4c670f45932d2225785090a0b04539537b7eba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\pi}{2} \\cos(x) = \\mathcal{A}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"107\" height=\"34\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/5/4c574667c037d58cdf1e7dbaa0d1eb0c88ff5958.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\pi}{2} \\sin(x) = \\mathcal{B}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"103\" height=\"34\" />. Then, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/6/65636b66ca89f7b8c8aa4443957add0e93fae9a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin(\\mathcal{A}) = \\cos({\\mathcal{B}})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"128\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>Aha! We know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/9/4e9acf20de9ac5bab6411b30806f065168ebf335.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right) = \\cos\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"151\" height=\"35\" />! So, the solution set to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/7/0b7bf42db84e4d2dbb7bf55476c12bf9f6233bc5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathcal{A}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/2/382cea990fadd43376cf42e8e0597a5eb13a67c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathcal{B}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"12\" height=\"13\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/b/4ab55cab2c6dfeeb0ad2f70e425dcf717499ab7d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(\\mathcal{A},\\mathcal{B}) = \\frac{\\pi}{4} + \\pi k : k \\in \\mathbb{Z}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"193\" height=\"34\" />.\n</p><p>Now, we substitute the values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/7/0b7bf42db84e4d2dbb7bf55476c12bf9f6233bc5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathcal{A}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/2/382cea990fadd43376cf42e8e0597a5eb13a67c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathcal{B}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"12\" height=\"13\" />, primarily, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/9/08985694eb667e303b622c19e1c24457edf4ebca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\pi}{2} \\cos(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"69\" height=\"34\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/d/97df26d3f50f5fc3480d9f681a6bf0677b36ac1b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\pi}{2} \\sin(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"67\" height=\"34\" /> respectively. We then have the two equalities:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/e/6de13489640326f5f5af4f1b3bb5bcc2bcc150fe.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\cos(x) = \\frac{\\pi}{4} + \\pi k : k \\in \\mathbb{Z}\\]\" width=\"206\" height=\"32\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/1/0d1098821c328379fc08f19abe05e8c8ba70e9ba.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\sin(x) = \\frac{\\pi}{4} + \\pi k : k \\in \\mathbb{Z}\\]\" width=\"204\" height=\"32\" />\n</p><p>In which multiplying by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/0/f80c5dddbc62faa2e29515da4b433c4c8dc9613f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2}{\\pi}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"13\" height=\"37\" /> on both sides rewards us with\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/e/a3e69d16eb9e2cd3d2a5e4f83495cc1bf804f2bf.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\cos(x) = \\frac{1}{2} + 2k : k \\in \\mathbb{Z}\\]\" width=\"186\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/e/43e039e3fe09d8958eb89893c3b53ca31500edb0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sin(x) = \\frac{1}{2} + 2k : k \\in \\mathbb{Z}\\]\" width=\"184\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>Aha! The values between the interval <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/e/ece27ba559bd93cdf2416aa0f88fc8d7d85e5791.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[0,\\pi]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"40\" height=\"20\" /> lie when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/d/badf0ecd1ef8289387d8462393438c6e2710ff28.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k=0$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" /> (because we originally had <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/f/caff2adb7e26dbf78a80dad660ae2e811dd2459b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\pi k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"23\" height=\"14\" />, so setting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/f/00fab47c0b9d0ce398d03e57d6720129d53434f2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" /> results in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/c/f2ca003a7da0de4994b4733e203b74ff52d42553.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\pi$\" width=\"10\" height=\"8\" />, in which because we have the value <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/9/2f960094315d60883495f9b74148e17487ee9584.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> at the right, we obtain <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/d/e6d73cd3e5a2a5af62722d67a78a9bfd9cc58ecf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2} + \\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"48\" height=\"38\" />, which is beyond the interval end bound <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/c/f2ca003a7da0de4994b4733e203b74ff52d42553.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\pi$\" width=\"10\" height=\"8\" />, so the only values that lie within that interval are when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/d/badf0ecd1ef8289387d8462393438c6e2710ff28.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k=0$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" />). Simplification results in\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/c/12c5bf5d64fc58ce6c7f463320d1cc879423f240.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\cos(x)=\\frac{1}{2}\\]\" width=\"84\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/f/44f7d24efb142bad72a0ec12bfab5a77006d057c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sin(x)=\\frac{1}{2}\\]\" width=\"82\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>The solutions to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/d/ced3ca016282db7a1810e8c0fa581e38b8af6867.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin(x)=\\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"86\" height=\"38\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/8/c28c86fd123f9e096ddf6e4339ce10952377ba73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x= \\frac{\\pi}{6} + \\pi k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"95\" height=\"34\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/e/f3edf86866d9bc3d9388acf12fc2ac9ef7b0d3fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x= \\frac{5\\pi}{6} + \\pi k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"104\" height=\"38\" />. We negate <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/9/539aa4de1aea85b3872297fe7586088424378af4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{5\\pi}{6} + \\pi k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"69\" height=\"38\" /> because that is not in the interval <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/1/0a151f5b93ce5735f72cdd79c46051f52b9d820d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[0, \\pi]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"36\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Looking at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/5/735b84b4f1769ff21f8318b2d2618698e87fc6a4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos(x)=\\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"88\" height=\"38\" />, the solutions are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/f/8dfb0bffe2ca1b6ec9acdf244b9a6f628b3be41d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\pi}{3} + \\pi k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"60\" height=\"34\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/8/61808a2fa819220c64feecb2cfbf1ff2ba8a03ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{5\\pi}{3} + \\pi k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"69\" height=\"38\" />. Again, we negate <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/8/61808a2fa819220c64feecb2cfbf1ff2ba8a03ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{5\\pi}{3} + \\pi k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"69\" height=\"38\" /> as it is not in the interval <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/e/ece27ba559bd93cdf2416aa0f88fc8d7d85e5791.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[0,\\pi]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"40\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>Now, we have one more thing to consider. The equality condition. Hmm, the two values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> seem to be different... Does this affect the equation to have no solutions?\n</p><p>No! Notice how we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/9/799dfb06e3ace7555fafb18ee57d62809fb6ceb9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin(\\cos(x)) = \\cos(\\sin(y))$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"196\" height=\"20\" />! Additionally, notice how <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/4/9c4a79b1daf344ddd9f92875be0e51c0ed570b01.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\pi}{2} - \\frac{\\pi}{6} = \\frac{\\pi}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"93\" height=\"34\" />! Now, assume <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/b/2cb62f20e5cb22c9c8a333344b4ef354b63ddee1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x= \\frac{\\pi}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"51\" height=\"34\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/d/efde102367b7c6bf904411ae1e15a4d5a2879b50.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=\\frac{\\pi}{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"51\" height=\"34\" />. We already know <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/2/5b26d60403ed92f89db8f602450aacbe5a0d1ccf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin(x)=\\cos(90-x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"159\" height=\"18\" />! So, we just have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/2/7f2c700572ddbc11eac965746f14b03665fc2382.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos(\\cos(x))=\\cos(\\cos(\\frac{\\pi}{2}-y))$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"237\" height=\"34\" />, but <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/e/94e523ae1befe5ec98c0c885dadbceb6910981f3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\pi}{2}-y=x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"83\" height=\"34\" />! So, we achieve <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/0/410bb0fa880b96030a4583526d8e8e9c590cce28.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos(\\cos(x)) = \\cos(\\cos(x))$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"201\" height=\"20\" />, which is always true!\n</p><p>Thus, any solution to this equation is in the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/a/a3a604c92fb8d22af56317f82bb22a7a3db8b1d7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x= \\frac{\\pi}{6} + \\pi k, \\frac{\\pi}{3} + \\pi k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"161\" height=\"34\" />.\n</p><p>To obtain the degree measure over the interval <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/e/ece27ba559bd93cdf2416aa0f88fc8d7d85e5791.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[0,\\pi]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"40\" height=\"20\" />, we must have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/d/badf0ecd1ef8289387d8462393438c6e2710ff28.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k=0$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" />. So, we achieve the values <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/0/9e0f4bbb8d84a7c6fade54fcd612db08ec5da7df.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=\\frac{\\pi}{6}, \\frac{\\pi}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"75\" height=\"34\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/0/fc03b0aaf66cf0ba97d33db5254ad0e92823c740.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x= 30^\\circ, 60^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"96\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/3/f530eb4e1a2b7f21a225ce5427c1f2707014f560.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(C) }2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"55\" height=\"28\" /> values that satisfy the equation.\n</p><p>~Pinotation\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Cofunction_Identity.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Cofunction_Identity)\">Solution 3 (Cofunction Identity)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Cofunction Identity)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>By the Cofunction Identity <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/e/edea7589a92ee46bd4339c89602575495394b0f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos\\theta=\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{2}-\\theta\\right),$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"163\" height=\"35\" /> we rewrite the given equation: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/e/06e3540d357c76e8d482f1816252689b9d0e734f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sin \\left(\\frac{\\pi}2 \\cos x\\right) = \\sin \\left(\\frac{\\pi}2 - \\frac{\\pi}2 \\sin x\\right).\\]\" width=\"270\" height=\"33\" />\nRecall that if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/1/4616fba077ff898c16f097cc6cb29082ad5260a5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin\\theta=\\sin\\phi,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"102\" height=\"18\" /> then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/6/e5624f86a55c8f35de05341cd18611f6f4058a93.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta=\\phi+2n\\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"99\" height=\"18\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/a/26ae46445598a86cb045c5b3d454f255f51d21d7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta=\\pi-\\phi+2n\\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"132\" height=\"18\" /> for some integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/9/bd923e41635af40a1abe58f230732f2280b0723a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> Therefore, we have two cases:\n</p>\n<ol style=\"margin-left: 1.5em;\">\n  <li><b><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/0/3b0dd23260e361e257cebe5a87232006ffcd0111.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boldsymbol{\\frac{\\pi}2 \\cos x = \\left(\\frac{\\pi}2 - \\frac{\\pi}2 \\sin x\\right) + 2n\\pi}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"286\" height=\"45\" /> for some integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/e/5ae62c78f41054a2b7d6d005ceabda2fcffc97a5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boldsymbol{n}$\" width=\"12\" height=\"8\" /></b> <p>\nWe rearrange and simplify: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/7/5d77e5720cff52ea5b14fa3c610c4e3e27b05dc4.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sin x + \\cos x = 1 + 4n.\\]\" width=\"174\" height=\"13\" />\nBy rough constraints, we know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/c/03c1b6d24d272ea881b76db992ea0ce1f0160493.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-2 &lt; \\sin x + \\cos x &lt; 2,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"180\" height=\"15\" /> from which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/a/cca71c59d8b304793a2edb4a2dbe3b859e236cfd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-2 &lt; 1 - 4n &lt; 2.$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"135\" height=\"12\" /> The only possibility is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/c/49c77b43dead6ba5c73bf22e1c33665cfb346fde.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=0,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"48\" height=\"16\" /> so\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/0/0b0bb18bf7c5c9c806eadd9f02bf145e934bb977.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} \\sin x + \\cos x &amp;= 1 &amp;&amp; (*) \\\\ \\sin^2 x + \\cos^2 x + 2\\sin x \\cos x &amp;= 1 \\\\ 2\\sin x \\cos x &amp;= 0 \\\\ \\sin(2x) &amp;= 0 \\\\ 2x &amp;= k\\pi \\\\ x &amp;= \\frac{k\\pi}{2} \\end{align*}\" width=\"353\" height=\"166\" />\nfor some integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/4/5d48e0968a64d782fe75bca620ce749938b7d0bb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k.$\" width=\"13\" height=\"12\" /> </p><p>\nWe get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/d/2fdb27c23d551e1bd306d971f763a15e69350168.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=0,\\frac{\\pi}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"65\" height=\"33\" /> for this case. Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/8/94816ab8a73eb77d27708b62b38cea1840d30ae9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=\\pi$\" width=\"45\" height=\"8\" /> is an extraneous solution by squaring <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/7/82754472eae3912d19b2a4e712c87b08635b4df4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(*).$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"26\" height=\"18\" /></p></li><p class=\"mw-empty-elt\">\n  </p><li><b><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/f/3cf12a06c78ef71ae8f64548fa0992c5891bdcc3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boldsymbol{\\frac{\\pi}2 \\cos x = \\pi - \\left(\\frac{\\pi}2 - \\frac{\\pi}2 \\sin x\\right) + 2n\\pi}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"325\" height=\"45\" /> for some integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/e/5ae62c78f41054a2b7d6d005ceabda2fcffc97a5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boldsymbol{n}$\" width=\"12\" height=\"8\" /></b> <p>\nSimilar to Case 1, we conclude that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/c/49c77b43dead6ba5c73bf22e1c33665cfb346fde.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=0,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"48\" height=\"16\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/3/693d045cac17bba7e6edad4d9de233911c010433.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\cos x - \\sin x = 1.\\]\" width=\"132\" height=\"12\" />\nWe get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/e/34ea5b6f6de584d56d19a89cc4923a9d9a5cfa41.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=0$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" /> for this case.</p></li><p class=\"mw-empty-elt\">\n</p></ol>\n<p>Together, we obtain <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/3/f530eb4e1a2b7f21a225ce5427c1f2707014f560.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(C) }2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"55\" height=\"28\" /> solutions: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/c/7dc5714b3c48ff5a5eb78996b2c48f7cd0d80106.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=0,\\frac{\\pi}{2}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"74\" height=\"34\" />\n</p><p>~MRENTHUSIASM\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_4_.28Graphs_and_Analyses.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4_(Graphs_and_Analyses)\">Solution 4 (Graphs and Analyses)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4 (Graphs and Analyses)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>This problem is equivalent to counting the intersections of the graphs of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/2/9626ce623bc6819a91efe910270dee7ce2fc3f3e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\cos x\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"138\" height=\"35\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/f/58f7fecb17b6cab35e4e3794d9963e6baab1e5ad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\sin x\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"138\" height=\"35\" /> in the closed interval <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/c/b4ccb3ab0522405552f4590e118eccf217cce9c4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[0,\\pi].$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"41\" height=\"18\" /> We construct a table of values, as shown below:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/d/bcd742d378458e46b475f233696e281083331b63.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\begin{array}{c|ccc} &amp; &amp; &amp; \\\\ [-2ex] &amp; \\boldsymbol{x=0} &amp; \\boldsymbol{x=\\frac{\\pi}{2}} &amp; \\boldsymbol{x=\\pi} \\\\ [1.5ex] \\hline &amp; &amp; &amp; \\\\ [-1ex] \\boldsymbol{\\cos x} &amp; 1 &amp; 0 &amp; -1 \\\\ [1.5ex] \\boldsymbol{\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\cos x} &amp; \\frac{\\pi}{2} &amp; 0 &amp; -\\frac{\\pi}{2} \\\\ [1.5ex] \\boldsymbol{\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\cos x\\right)} &amp; 1 &amp; 0 &amp; -1 \\\\ [1.5ex] \\hline  &amp; &amp; &amp; \\\\ [-1ex] \\boldsymbol{\\sin x} &amp; 0 &amp; 1 &amp; 0 \\\\ [1.5ex] \\boldsymbol{\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\sin x} &amp; 0 &amp; \\frac{\\pi}{2} &amp; 0 \\\\ [1.5ex] \\boldsymbol{\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\sin x\\right)} &amp; 1 &amp; 0 &amp; 1 \\\\ [1ex] \\end{array}\\]\" width=\"329\" height=\"246\" />\nFor <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/2/192702db67df074a645d5ad546b648098199dfef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x\\in[0,\\pi],$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"78\" height=\"20\" /> note that:\n</p>\n<ul><li><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/f/a5fa15ed83f755f18132063b8f690810b0f0bb62.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\cos x\\in\\left[-\\frac{\\pi}{2},\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\right],$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"157\" height=\"35\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/6/b367dc6c6b993f327240033cf658d12f29951b78.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\cos x\\right)\\in[-1,1].$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"182\" height=\"35\" /></li></ul>\n<ul><li><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/a/b4a2bdb76ba5f3ea6721f944da15f1554f6fc1ba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\sin x\\in\\left[0,\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\right],$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"135\" height=\"35\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/7/9c7d2a68cf4efebf6cd0fd0d71257fe1d475100b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\sin x\\right)\\in[0,1].$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"168\" height=\"35\" /></li></ul>\n<p>For the graphs to intersect, we need <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/8/418052bfbadf2ff056f256e0574a002ad15809d0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\cos x\\right)\\in[0,1].$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"168\" height=\"35\" /> This occurs when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/f/f8ff205fc6994a190cc833ceff7e81a464f8298c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\cos x\\in\\left[0,\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\right].$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"137\" height=\"35\" />\n</p><p>By the Cofunction Identity <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/e/edea7589a92ee46bd4339c89602575495394b0f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos\\theta=\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{2}-\\theta\\right),$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"163\" height=\"35\" /> we rewrite the given equation:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/6/ee6ed0735ea791a9591bb2ee0eda6a1e50923cd0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\cos x\\right) = \\sin\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{2}-\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\sin x\\right).\\]\" width=\"270\" height=\"33\" />\nSince <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/5/0b59b91069bf74a053ed6d23c2f2366575e64d00.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\cos x\\in\\left[0,\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\right]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"129\" height=\"35\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/a/b4a2bdb76ba5f3ea6721f944da15f1554f6fc1ba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\sin x\\in\\left[0,\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\right],$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"135\" height=\"35\" /> it follows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/6/ad6d7672d2ef0d27254045d666d8a9cd52e94f59.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x\\in\\left[0,\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\right]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"83\" height=\"35\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/4/a34b74443d671784a6bd431e59c2453b5e0e1b72.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\pi}{2}-\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\sin x\\in\\left[0,\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\right].$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"172\" height=\"35\" />\n</p><p>We can apply the arcsine function to both sides, then rearrange and simplify:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/1/5c1476de5a7750200666c73ca1b3d53112ef7aae.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} \\frac{\\pi}{2}\\cos x &amp;= \\frac{\\pi}{2}-\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\sin x \\\\ \\sin x + \\cos x &amp;= 1. \\end{align*}\" width=\"210\" height=\"54\" />\nFrom Case 1 in Solution 2, we conclude that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/1/be11a56a55425d6c6b69f70f5fa98eab95e8ad18.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0,1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/7/05734201836e943797bbde2c49d634ac14b0a009.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{2},0\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"50\" height=\"33\" /> are the only points of intersection, as shown below:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/b/a5bb3fda3e60884de1b737e849a42cf5879ecf05.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] /* Made by MRENTHUSIASM */ size(600,200);   real f(real x) { return sin(pi/2*cos(x)); }  real g(real x) { return cos(pi/2*sin(x)); }  draw(graph(f,0,pi),red,&quot;$y=\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\cos x\\right)$&quot;); draw(graph(g,0,pi),blue,&quot;$y=\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\sin x\\right)$&quot;);  real xMin = 0; real xMax = 5/4*pi; real yMin = -2; real yMax = 2;  //Draws the horizontal gridlines void horizontalLines() {   for (real i = yMin+1; i &lt; yMax; ++i)   {     draw((xMin,i)--(xMax,i), mediumgray+linewidth(0.4));   } }  //Draws the vertical gridlines void verticalLines() {   for (real i = xMin+pi/2; i &lt; xMax; i+=pi/2)   {     draw((i,yMin)--(i,yMax), mediumgray+linewidth(0.4));   } }  //Draws the horizontal ticks void horizontalTicks() {   for (real i = yMin+1; i &lt; yMax; ++i)   {     draw((-1/8,i)--(1/8,i), black+linewidth(1));   } }  //Draws the vertical ticks void verticalTicks() {   for (real i = xMin+pi/2; i &lt; xMax; i+=pi/2)   {     draw((i,-1/8)--(i,1/8), black+linewidth(1));   } }  horizontalLines(); verticalLines(); horizontalTicks(); verticalTicks(); draw((xMin,0)--(xMax,0),black+linewidth(1.5),EndArrow(5)); draw((0,yMin)--(0,yMax),black+linewidth(1.5),EndArrow(5)); label(&quot;$x$&quot;,(xMax,0),(2,0)); label(&quot;$y$&quot;,(0,yMax),(0,2));  pair A[]; A[0] = (pi/2,0); A[1] = (pi,0); A[2] = (0,1); A[3] = (0,0); A[4] = (0,-1);  label(&quot;$\\frac{\\pi}{2}$&quot;,A[0],(0,-2.5)); label(&quot;$\\pi$&quot;,A[1],(0,-2.5)); label(&quot;$1$&quot;,A[2],(-2.5,0)); label(&quot;$0$&quot;,A[3],(-2.5,0)); label(&quot;$-1$&quot;,A[4],(-2.5,0));  dot((0,1),linewidth(5));  dot((pi/2,0),linewidth(5));   add(legend(),point(E),40E,UnFill); [/asy]\" width=\"678\" height=\"335\" />\nTherefore, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/c/08c183761fd0ecf4de322d4dfd5af3320bce4bbe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(C) }2}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"59\" height=\"28\" />\n</p><p>~MRENTHUSIASM (credit given to TheAMCHub)\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_5_.28No_Graphing.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5_(No_Graphing)\">Solution 5 (No Graphing)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5 (No Graphing)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/c/69c143db617b951256d8fcb4041df246eb06a43f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin(a) = \\cos(b),$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"123\" height=\"20\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> must be complementary angles, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/e/55e5a87476c3af0503c6a0473d2e301217c7ed16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a + b = \\frac{\\pi}{2}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"86\" height=\"34\" /> So we have \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/5/ab5f0b51b0366a01ebec54aab7f1d51f15f05d04.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{\\pi}{2}(\\sin(x) + \\cos(x)) = \\frac{\\pi}{2} \\implies \\sin(x) + \\cos(x) = 1.\\]\" width=\"388\" height=\"32\" /> \n</p><p>We know <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/f/2ef566b707cab77b14933f162ed7d8b00078152d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin^2(x) + \\cos^2(x) = 1,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"173\" height=\"22\" /> so we can express <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/3/c938e3f9dea789595c6290070f7975f45bc4300a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"47\" height=\"18\" /> in terms of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/1/081bf0417da2140657aad909a14ca6c3ff8b77d5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"45\" height=\"18\" /> and set those expressions equal to each other: \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/e/c2e7717f748673ec45c120896908f3151dad437f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sqrt{1 - \\sin^2(x)} = 1 - \\sin(x) \\implies 1 - \\sin^2(x) = (1 - \\sin(x))^2 \\implies \\sin(x) = 1.\\]\" width=\"572\" height=\"32\" /> \n</p><p>So now the problem becomes the number of values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> on the interval <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/1/0a151f5b93ce5735f72cdd79c46051f52b9d820d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[0, \\pi]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"36\" height=\"18\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/9/b49b8165ca139ed62115b63ff38b3544dd38871c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin(x) = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"82\" height=\"20\" />. It's pretty easy to see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> can equal <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/5/e25523ad869caf448d31d6f06cdbca4d6d60070f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\pi}{2},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"19\" height=\"33\" /> so the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/c/08c183761fd0ecf4de322d4dfd5af3320bce4bbe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(C) }2}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"59\" height=\"28\" />\n</p><p>~<a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=User:Grogg007\" title=\"User:Grogg007\">grogg007</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn_.28Using_Triangle_Inequality_.26_Trigonometry.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn_(Using_Triangle_Inequality_&amp;_Trigonometry)\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn (Using Triangle Inequality &amp; Trigonometry)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by OmegaLearn (Using Triangle Inequality &amp; Trigonometry)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/wJxN1YPuyCg\">https://youtu.be/wJxN1YPuyCg</a>\n</p><p>~ pi_is_3.14\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_.28Quick_and_Easy.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_(Quick_and_Easy)\">Video Solution (Quick and Easy)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution (Quick and Easy)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/6AWb9cqFblU\">https://youtu.be/6AWb9cqFblU</a>\n</p><p>~Education, the Study of Everything\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A\" title=\"2021 AMC 12A\">2021 AMC 12A</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Problems\" title=\"2021 AMC 12A Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Answer_Key\" title=\"2021 AMC 12A Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2021 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 18\">Problem 18</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2021 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 20\">Problem 20</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2021 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2021 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2021 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2021 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2021 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2021 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2021 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2021 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2021 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2021 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2021 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2021 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2021 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2021 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2021 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2021 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"2021 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2021 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2021 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2021 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"2021 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"2021 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"2021 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"2021 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 25\">25</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AMC_12_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AMC 12 Problems and Solutions\"> All AMC 12 Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017141613\n